{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-26365",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14237394/assets/77adc8fb9c00bd21579a8697f8b11c228e3864e657f2b991be4d09b4c6f5a96d.png)\n\nSince $\\overset{\\to }{OD}$ is the bisector of $∠AOC$, we have \n\n$$\nm∠AOD=m∠DOC=4x.\n$$\n\nSince $\\overset{\\to }{OE}$ is the bisector of $∠BOC$, we have \n\n$$\nm∠EOB=m∠COE=5x.\n$$\n\nNow, by the angle addition postulate, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOD+m∠DOC+m∠EOB+m∠COE & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 4x+4x+5x+5x & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 18x & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={10}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
